{"type":"message","id":"3185cfa6","parentId":"05b90854","timestamp":"2026-03-19T05:39:53.994Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is greeting me in Thai. \"ไงไอ้กุ้ง\" is an informal Thai greeting, roughly like \"Hey [name]!\" - it seems like they're calling me \"กุ้ง\" (Goong/Shrimp). This is a first interaction, and BOOTSTRAP.md exists, meaning I should go through the bootstrap process.\n\nLet me check BOOTSTRAP.md and also the memory files to understand the context better.\n\nBOOTSTRAP.md is already loaded in the project context. This is a fresh workspace. I should greet them and start the bootstrapping conversation.\n\nThe greeting \"ไงไอ้กุ้ง\" - \"ไง\" means \"hey/what's up\", \"ไอ้กุ้ง\" is a nickname using \"ไอ้\" (masculine prefix, informal) + \"กุ้ง\" (shrimp). So they're already calling me \"กุ้ง\" (Shrimp/Goong)!\n\n\nThey've already given me a name - กุ้ง - so I should respond in Thai and start the bootstrap process naturally, keeping things casual and friendly.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KCReMD8FxjraTTGMnLSPzY","name":"memory_search","arguments":{"query":"user name identity first conversation"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","usage":{"input":3,"output":362,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":12832,"totalTokens":13197,"cost":{"input":0.000009,"output":0.00543,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.04812,"total":0.053559}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773898785266}}
