{"type":"message","id":"06cba9fc","parentId":"aa47b4f4","timestamp":"2026-03-19T13:51:25.885Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking if there's a way to run the dashboard automatically like how OpenClaw gateway runs. Let me think about this...\n\nOpenClaw gateway runs as a Windows service or similar. The user wants the dashboard to run similarly without needing to manually run it.\n\nFor Windows, the options are:\n1. Windows Service (using NSSM)\n2. Task Scheduler (what we tried)\n3. Startup folder\n\nThe simplest approach that doesn't need admin rights might be the Startup folder approach. Let me think...\n\nActually, the user is asking if OpenClaw has a built-in way to run it, similar to how gateway auto-starts. \n\nI should look into whether OpenClaw has a configuration option for auto-running commands, or suggest the startup folder method as a simpler alternative that avoids needing elevated permissions.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"มีสิ! ใช้ **Startup folder** ของ Windows ได้เลย ไม่ต้องสิทธิ์ admin\n\nกูสร้างไฟล์ให้เลย:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_019YJE257CJL1twct44uVo21","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\hp\\AppData\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\Startup\\dashboard.bat","content":"@echo off\ncd /d C:\\Users\\hp\\Projects\\dashboard\nstart /min \"\" powershell -WindowStyle Hidden -Command \"npx next dev --port 3000\"\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","usage":{"input":3,"output":390,"cacheRead":59948,"cacheWrite":355,"totalTokens":60696,"cost":{"input":0.000009,"output":0.00585,"cacheRead":0.017984399999999998,"cacheWrite":0.00133125,"total":0.025174649999999996}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773928276063}}
