{"type":"message","id":"ea52ecbc","parentId":"c866734f","timestamp":"2026-03-19T14:08:27.345Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"System: [2026-03-19 21:06:00 GMT+7] Exec completed (swift-sh, code 1) :: | +-----------------------------------------------------+ Config invalid File: ~\\.openclaw\\openclaw.json Problem: - auth.profiles.google:default: Unrecognized key: \"apiKey\" Run: o…\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Thu 2026-03-19 21:08 GMT+7] 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 อ่ะกูได้มาละของopenrouter"}],"timestamp":1773929307340}}
{"type":"message","id":"2135cd80","parentId":"ea52ecbc","timestamp":"2026-03-19T14:08:32.279Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me update the config to use OpenRouter instead of Google directly.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"โอเค แก้ให้เลย!"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KGUgYJRT2jU3BDibdNNcqh","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\hp\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\providers\\openrouter.md"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","usage":{"input":3,"output":125,"cacheRead":66945,"cacheWrite":462,"totalTokens":67535,"cost":{"input":0.000009,"output":0.0018750000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0200835,"cacheWrite":0.0017325,"total":0.023700000000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773929307344}}
{"type":"message","id":"9d0f98d3","parentId":"2135cd80","timestamp":"2026-03-19T14:08:32.373Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01KGUgYJRT2jU3BDibdNNcqh","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nsummary: \"Use OpenRouter's unified API to access many models in OpenClaw\"\nread_when:\n  - You want a single API key for many LLMs\n  - You want to run models via OpenRouter in OpenClaw\ntitle: \"OpenRouter\"\n---\n\n# OpenRouter\n\nOpenRouter provides a **unified API** that routes requests to many models behind a single\nendpoint and API key. It is OpenAI-compatible, so most OpenAI SDKs work by switching the base URL.\n\n## CLI setup\n\n```bash\nopenclaw onboard --auth-choice apiKey --token-provider openrouter --token \"$OPENROUTER_API_KEY\"\n```\n\n## Config snippet\n\n```json5\n{\n  env: { OPENROUTER_API_KEY: \"sk-or-...\" },\n  agents: {\n    defaults: {\n      model: { primary: \"openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5\" },\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Model refs are `openrouter/<provider>/<model>`.\n- For more model/provider options, see [/concepts/model-providers](/concepts/model-providers).\n- OpenRouter uses a Bearer token with your API key under the hood.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773929312370}}
