{"type":"message","id":"07c96013","parentId":"5b124ef6","timestamp":"2026-03-19T14:54:25.438Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Verifying Gemini Model Names**\n\nI've hit a snag, it seems the model name I was using for Gemini via OpenRouter is wrong. The agent gave me an \"unknown model\" error. I need to double-check the OpenRouter documentation to get the correct, supported model names.\n\n\n**Confirming Gemini Model Names**\n\nI'm now certain that the previous model name was incorrect. My agent returned an \"Unknown model\" error, so I'm investigating supported Gemini model names within OpenRouter. Based on OpenRouter's documentation, I suspect the issue is with the specific Gemini model ID format, and I'm updating the model name in the agent to include it.\n\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"โทษทีๆ มันมีปัญหาที่ชื่อ model ของ Gemini บน OpenRouter! 😅\n\nOpenRouter มันจะใช้ชื่อ model แปลกๆ หน่อย กูจะเช็คให้ว่า Gemini 2.5 flash/pro ชื่ออะไรแน่ แล้วแก้ให้เลย\n\nรอแป๊บนึงนะ 🦞","textSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"web_search_1773932062471_1","name":"web_search","arguments":{"query":"OpenRouter available Gemini models"}}],"api":"google-generative-ai","provider":"google","model":"gemini-2.5-flash","usage":{"input":58707,"output":234,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":58941,"cost":{"input":0.0176121,"output":0.000585,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.018197099999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773932056920}}
